The problem with using the Hessian naively is that it might improve things locally while making it worse everywhere else.  What we really want is an average of the Hessian across parameter space which brings us back to the global covariance which we're estimating empirically already.  Remember, there's only ever one option which is an expectation with respect to the posterior!

